    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d340">

                <pb facs="0510" n="1974" sameAs="frus:frus1951v06p2/pg1974"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">689.90D/5–2351: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Pakistan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Warren</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Karachi</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-05-23T12:00:00+05:30">May 23,
                            1951—noon.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1109. I conveyed to FonMin yesterday afternoon
                    Dept’s position re para 1 Ikramullah ltr, May 15, Deptel 755, May 18. Zafrulla said it was mot in his opinion
                    intention GOP to project US as arbiter of
                    agreement but only to satisfy itself as to Dept attitude shld GOA persist in <pb facs="0511" n="1975"
                        xml:id="pg1975"/> its proPushtoonistan propaganda. I reiterated sense of
                    first sentence ref Deptel and Zafrulla said
                    he wld clarify matter with PM.</p>
                <p>Be memo May 15 Zafrulla said it was not his understanding that GOP intended to preclude Pak Amb at Kabul from discussing matters of common concern and that
                    he wld also clarify this understanding with PM.</p>
                <p>Zafrulla then expressed hope that we wld now come to final agreement on text of
                        Pak acceptance and suggested that that shld
                    be the case assuming PM confirms his (Zafrulla’s)
                    understanding of GOP intent as expressed
                    above.</p>
                <p>I recommend to Dept that if PM approves Zafrulla’s
                    statement of intent and understanding on both points raised ref Deptel that we tell GOP that their May 15 memo will be transmitted to GOA as constituting Pak acceptance our <hi rendition="#italic">démarche</hi>.</p>
                <p>Dept pass London; sent Dept 1109, rptd info Kabul 60, London 78.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Warren</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
